[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'What if you could edit any video as easily as editing a sentence? Change clothes, replace objects, insert completely new elements, transform an entire scene, generate images, create text-to-video, reference-to-video,'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video-to-video, and much, much more using just a single model while keeping the motion and temporal consistency intact. That\'s exactly what ByteDance\'s new open-source'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model, Bernini, is trying to achieve. Now, Bernini isn\'t just another AI video model. Instead of relying purely on diffusion, it first uses a powerful'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'multimodal AI planner to understand exactly what needs to be changed inside the video. And then, a dedicated renderer generates the final result. This two-stage approach gives it'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'incredibly accurate edits, much stronger identity preservation, better object consistency, and significantly improved temporal consistency throughout the'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video. So, for this tutorial, I\'ve created a complete ComfyUI workflow for Bernini. If you want to use the exact same workflow, you can download it completely free from my Patreon page.'

